# 밥친구 — shared storage
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the two VITE_ values from the
# Supabase dashboard (Project Settings → API). With both set, tables are
# shared between devices; with either missing the app falls back to
# localStorage and keeps working on one device, so a developer without keys
# can still run everything — tests, audit and build included.
#
# The anon key is designed to be public and ships inside the browser bundle.
# That is safe *because* row level security is enabled in supabase/schema.sql
# — run that file before pointing the app at a new project, or the key
# becomes a licence for anyone to delete the pilot's tables.

# ── Local development ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These two, and nothing else, belong in .env.local.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Build-time only, on the machine that fetches the register ───────────
# Deliberately NOT prefixed VITE_. Vite exposes only VITE_* to the browser,
# so the name is the guarantee that this stays on the machine running
# `node scripts/seoul-food-api.mjs` and never reaches a bundle. Not needed to
# develop or deploy the app — the 8,118 places are already in the repo.
# Get your own at data.go.kr, dataset 15097605 (free, a minute or two).

SEOUL_FOOD_API_KEY=

# ── NOT here: Edge Function secrets ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# These three are set in the Supabase dashboard under Edge Functions →
# Secrets, and must never be written into this file or .env.local. They are
# listed by name so that somebody looking for them knows where they live,
# and knows that finding them absent here is correct rather than missing.
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   bypasses row level security entirely. This
#                               file is read by client-side code; a service
#                               key here is the whole database published.
#   GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD          sends mail as the team account.
#   RESEND_API_KEY              the alternative sender, if a domain arrives.
#
# See supabase/functions/send-notifications/SETUP.md.
